 17592186045417] [17592186064033 #edb/ref 1069 "e-258" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064033 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $g(x)$ is given by\n![](images/c6/c67122865cc8decbb3238cd70c1fe662bdbcf9f697bd8a8e594e4408b88a08c3.svg)\nIf $g(x)$ is continuous at $x=2,$ what is the value $b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064033 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e6c4219b-1955-5fa0-a362-6cc273510d88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064033 #edb/ref 1074 "From the definition of $g(x)$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}g(x)={lim}_{x\\to 2}(\\sqrt{bx+3})=\\sqrt{2b+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=2,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}g(x) & =g(2) \\\\ \\sqrt{2b+3} & =5 \\\\ 2b+3 & =25 \\\\ 2b & =22 \\\\ b & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064034 #edb/ref 1069 "e-259" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064034 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $h(x)$ is given by\n![](images/d1/d113c9de6e0c7946ed9952a2a245f4ba0ebb627b74c4661a2a067216fe5099d8.svg)\n\nGiven that $h(x)$ is continuous at $x=0,$ what is the value of $c?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064034 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b411bf9f-f944-505d-94dc-13df743545dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064034 #edb/ref 1074 "From the definition of $h(x),$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}h(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}{log}_{3}⁡(x+c) \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡(0+c) \\\\  & ={log}_{3}⁡(c).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $h(x)$ to be continuous at $x=0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}h(x) & =h(0) \\\\ {log}_{3}⁡(c) & =2 \\\\ c & ={3}^{2} \\\\ c & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $c=9$ removes the point discontinuity." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064118 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6320" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064118 #edb/ref 1071 "The function $f(x)$ is defined for every real number $x$ and is given by\n![](images/90/90209edc9ee3cc9c6c17b71427dc4dda0a14558a9df7b2a71dbe017073b9086a.svg)\nIf $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1,$ what is the value of $k?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064118 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5443849c-193c-58a9-ae6c-1b859bbd1d4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064118 #edb/ref 1074 "From the definition of $f(x),$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,1}({x}^{2}+2kx+1) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}+2k(1)+1 \\\\  & =2+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=1,$ we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x) & =f(1) \\\\ 2+2k & =4 \\\\ 2k & =2 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting $k=1$ removes the point discontinuity." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064150 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048784 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504621 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064150 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064150 #edb/ref 1039 "Removing a Point Discontinuity in a Piecewise Radical Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064150 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186064033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064150 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "40d01201-07ca-5083-a7f8-095be503df27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064151 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064151 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064151 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064151 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064151 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064151 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186504603 #edb/ref 1